															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/voct" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(392303); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=392303&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608843990" alt="Voct" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=392303)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/voct" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(392303); return false;" >Voct</a></span> <span class="odate time_1264519293 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">26 Jan 2010 15:21</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-684545">
									

<p>I don't see why its effect on human skin is to become super-adhesive.</p>
<p>These things make &lt;any system to which they are applied&gt; work at 110% of its optimum efficiency, yes?</p>
<p>And it's not limited to <em>a single characteristic of that system</em> - note the computer being boosted to 110% of multiple non-dependent traits.</p>
<p>If it's ineffective on biological systems, then… why is it bonding with the skin?</p>
<p>Or is it that the sticker bonds permanently with anything to which it's applied? If so, why is this only discovered during testing on a live subject?</p>
<p>And if not, what happens to a system from which the sticker is removed?</p>
<p>If we apply the sticker to &lt;a piece of a system&gt;, boost the system, then remove the sticker-adorned piece and put it in a <em>different</em> system… what happens to the second system?</p>
<p>What if the sticker-adorned piece is used for a different purpose in the second system?</p>
<p>What happens if we put 2 stickers on a single surface?</p>
<p>What happens if we cut one of these in half? Will a half-sticker boost a system by 5%? Will it damp a system to 55%?</p>

							</div>

								
					
